\": null, \"evidence\": \"Emma marked prod-1 Sold and deleted prod-5; buyer-side browse then showed '8 items available' with prod-1 and prod-5 absent (previously 10). Neither is reachable from browse, categories or search, so neither can be added to a cart or used to start a purchase request. Earlier, a self-created listing marked Sold likewise disappeared from browse ('QA Crate' → 0 items available).\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-5\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Registered 'QA Buyer' / qa.buyer@example.com / qapass123 / Austin, TX → toast 'Account created successfully!', redirected to home, header shows user menu + Sell + cart (signed in). Password shorter than 6 chars is blocked by minlength validation.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-6\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"No maximum-price filter: the price range slider exposes only a 'Minimum' thumb\", \"actual\": \"The Price Range control renders a single Radix thumb with aria-label='Minimum' (aria-valuemin=0, aria-valuemax=500); the displayed range '$0 - $500' has no second/max thumb, so a buyer cannot cap the maximum price. Other filters combine correctly (Furniture + New + Upcycled-only → exactly prod-10 $320 and prod-3 $175; min price $100 + distance ≤12mi → 5 items all ≥$100 and ≤12mi) and sorts by price low→high ($35…$320) and distance (2.5→12mi) are correct.\", \"evidence\": \"document.querySelectorAll(\\\"[data-semtag-id='browse.filters.price'] [role=slider]\\\").length === 1, aria-label 'Minimum'.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-7\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"'wood' → 3 results (Reclaimed Wood Bookshelf title, Mid-Century Armchair description 'wood frame', Kids Wooden Train Set); 'PORTLAND' (uppercase) → 3 Portland, OR listings; clearing the box restored 10 items available.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-8\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Signed-in QA Buyer added prod-1 (Emma's, $285) twice → cart badge stayed 1 (no duplicate), then added prod-9 ($35). Cart shows 2 items with title, photo, location (Brooklyn, NY / Austin, TX) and price; total $320.00 = 285+35.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-9\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Signed-in QA Buyer opened 'Send a message to Emma Green' on prod-1 (not owned, available); Send button disabled while empty; after typing a message it sent with toast 'Message sent to seller!' and the dialog closed.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-21\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Category selection from the Categories page does not filter browse results\", \"actual\": \"Clicking 'Home Decor' (card states '2 items') navigated to /?category=home-decor, but the browse grid still showed all 10 listings, the count read '10 items available', and every category filter toggle remained aria-checked=false — the category query parameter is ignored.\", \"evidence\": \"URL /?category=home-decor; browse.count = '10 items available'; 10 product cards across all categories rendered.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-22\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Sellers have no way to view purchase requests or buyer messages\", \"actual\": \"Buyer marcus@example.com sent a message 'QA-TEST-MSG-42…' on Emma's prod-1 and then a cart purchase request for prod-1 + prod-5 (toast 'Purchase requests sent to sellers!'). Signing in as the seller emma@example.com, /my-listings shows only listing rows (title, price, status, View/Mark Sold/Delete) with no requests or messages, the owner's product detail page shows no request/message section (page text does not contain 'QA-TEST-MSG-42'), and the only other seller destination, 'My Profile' (/profile), renders the 404 'Page not found' screen. The cart request is therefore reported as sent with no recorded request the seller can view.\", \"evidence\": \"Seller UI contains no requests view; /profile is a 404 route.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-10\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Login with nobody.unregistered@example.com rejected: 'Invalid credentials. Try: emma@example.com', stayed on /login, no session created.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-11\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Registering 'EMMA@Example.com' (case variant of existing emma@example.com) rejected with 'An account with this email already exists'; no session created, stayed on /register.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-12\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Password is never verified; any password authenticates a registered account\", \"actual\": \"Account qa.buyer@example.com was registered with password 'qapass123'. Logging in with 'TotallyWrongPassword999' succeeded: toast 'Welcome back!', redirect to home, header shows the signed-in user menu. The login page itself advertises 'Demo accounts: ... (any password works)'.\", \"evidence\": \"Login accepted an incorrect password and created an authenticated session.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-13\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"QA Buyer viewing Emma Green's prod-1 sees only Add to Cart / Message Seller (no Mark Sold, Delete or manage links); on their own listing prod-1787847297967 the buy controls are replaced by 'Manage Your Listings', and /my-listings lists only the signed-in seller's own listing with its management actions.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-14\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Empty submit blocked by native required validation on title/description/price/location ('Please fill out this field.'); missing photo → toast 'Please add at least one image'; missing category with all else filled → toast 'Please fill in all required fields'. No listing created in any case.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-15\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Price field is type=number min=0; submitting -50 blocked with 'Value must be greater than or equal to 0.' and no listing created; non